  "id": "reflexive-verben",
  "name": "Reflexive verbs: me levanto, se ducha",
  "level": "A2",
  "status": "geprueft",
  "variety": "es-ES",
  "es419": { "note": "Reflexive verbs work the same in Latin America. Os levantáis is Spain only: there people say ustedes se levantan." },
  "subtitle": "Many daily-routine verbs need a small pronoun that matches the person: me levanto, te duchas, se viste. In the dictionary the verb ends in -se: levantarse. The pronoun goes before the conjugated verb.",
  "briefMarks": ["me", "te", "se", "nos", "os", "-se"],
  "source": "icanspeak Spanish original text (grammar-a2 run, 2026-11-04)",
  "concept": {
    "flow": [
      { "text": "(no)" },
      { "text": "me · te · se · nos · os · se", "variant": "prep" },
      { "text": "levanto · duchas · viste", "variant": "verb" }
    ],
    "exampleHtml": "<span class=\"vp-prep\">Me</span> <span class=\"vp-verb\">levanto</span> a las seis. · Mi hijo <span class=\"vp-prep\">se</span> <span class=\"vp-verb\">ducha</span> por la noche. · ¿A qué hora <span class=\"vp-prep\">te</span> <span class=\"vp-verb\">acuestas</span>? · No <span class=\"vp-prep\">nos</span> <span class=\"vp-verb\">quedamos</span>.",
    "qa": [
      {
        "html": "The verb ends in <strong>-se</strong> in the dictionary: <em>levantarse, ducharse, llamarse</em>. When you use it, the pronoun moves <strong>in front</strong> and changes with the person: <em>me levanto, te levantas, se levanta, nos levantamos, os levantáis, se levantan</em>.",
        "tag": "The form"
      },
      {
        "html": "<strong>no</strong> goes before the pronoun: <em>No me levanto tarde.</em> With a question word, same order: <em>¿Cómo te llamas? ¿Cuándo os vais?</em>",
        "tag": "Order"
      },
      {
        "html": "With an <strong>infinitive</strong>, the pronoun goes on the end or before the first verb. It still matches the person: <em>Tengo que levantarme. = Me tengo que levantar. Vamos a sentarnos.</em>",
        "tag": "With an infinitive"
      },
      {
        "html": "Stem changes stay: <em>acostarse → me acuesto, despertarse → me despierto, vestirse → me visto, sentarse → me siento</em>.",
        "tag": "Stem change"
      },
      {
        "html": "For <strong>your own body and clothes</strong>, use <em>el, la, los, las</em>, not <em>mi</em>: <em>Me lavo las manos. Se pone el abrigo.</em>",
        "tag": "Body and clothes"
      },
      {
        "html": "The pronoun can change the meaning: <em>Lavo el coche</em> (the car) / <em>Me lavo</em> (myself). <em>Voy a casa</em> / <em>Me voy</em> (I'm leaving). <em>Llamo a Ana</em> / <em>Me llamo Ana</em>.",
        "tag": "With or without"
      }
    ],
    "noteHtml": "Common mistakes: ✗ <em>Levanto a las seis</em> → ✓ <em>Me levanto a las seis</em>. ✗ <em>Se levanto</em> → ✓ <em>Me levanto</em>. ✗ <em>Me lavo mis manos</em> → ✓ <em>Me lavo las manos</em>. ✗ <em>Tengo que levantarse</em> → ✓ <em>Tengo que levantarme</em>. ✗ <em>Me acosto</em> → ✓ <em>Me acuesto</em>.",
    "reference": {
